        comparison_points: ['Money Bill is narrowly defined and Speaker-certified; an ordinary Financial Bill can involve wider matters and has a different procedure.', 'Rajya Sabha can recommend on a Money Bill but has a full legislative role on an ordinary Bill.'],
        common_misconceptions: ['Rajya Sabha can veto a Money Bill by refusing to pass it.', 'Every Bill involving money is automatically a Money Bill under Article 110.'],
        exam_focus_points: ['Memorise the 14-day Rajya Sabha period.', 'Link Article 110 with Speaker certification and Article 112 with the Budget.', 'Compare Money Bill, Financial Bill and Appropriation Bill.']
