        comparison_points: ['No-confidence concerns whether the ministry survives; censure condemns a policy but does not automatically remove the ministry.', 'Question Hour is scheduled questioning; Zero Hour is an established practice for urgent matters.'],
        common_misconceptions: ['A no-confidence motion can be passed in Rajya Sabha to remove the Union ministry.', 'Zero Hour is a constitutional Article expressly named in the Constitution.'],
        exam_focus_points: ['Connect collective responsibility with Lok Sabha, not Rajya Sabha.', 'Revise question, confidence, censure and adjournment devices.', 'Understand that parliamentary control includes information, debate, finance and confidence.']
