        key_points: ['Onset near Kerala around early June', 'Arabian Sea branch', 'Bay of Bengal branch', 'Monsoon trough', 'Orographic rain and rain shadow.'],
        examples: ['Tracing the Bay branch to north India', 'Explaining a Western Ghats rain shadow'],
        comparison_points: ['Arabian Sea branch affects west coast and Ghats; Bay branch affects northeast and northern plains.', 'Active monsoon brings widespread rain; break monsoon is a temporary lull or redistribution.'],
        common_misconceptions: ['The monsoon arrives across India on one single day.', 'A break means the monsoon has permanently withdrawn.'],
        exam_focus_points: ['Map both branches.', 'Connect relief to windward and leeward rainfall.', 'Revise monsoon trough and break conditions.']
