      short_answer: { question: 'Explain the relationship between the President, Prime Minister and Parliament in the parliamentary executive.', expected_answer: 'The President is the constitutional head and normally acts on the aid and advice of the Council headed by the Prime Minister. The Prime Minister communicates decisions to the President, leads the government in Parliament and maintains Lok Sabha confidence. Parliament debates, legislates, controls finance and holds the ministry accountable.', explanation: 'The answer should combine formal authority, real executive leadership and parliamentary responsibility.' }
